  "notes": "EventBus Abstraction + Subscribe API implemented as specified.\n\n1. NEW: src/orchestra/event-bus.ts (~250 LoC) — EventBus class extending EventEmitter with:\n   - publish(event, sprintId?) — in-process event delivery with sprintId + channel filtering, exception swallowing\n   - subscribe(sprintId, channels, fn) — filtered subscription returning unsubscribe function\n   - tail(projectRoot, sprintId, n) — async JSONL tail reader for backfill\n   - watchFile(projectRoot, sprintId) — cross-process event detection via fs.watch with incremental offset reads\n   - unwatchAll() — cleanup all FSWatcher instances\n   - Singleton export: eventBus\n\n2. MODIFIED: src/orchestra/event-stream.ts — Added eventBus.publish(event, sprintId) after JSONL appendFileSync in writeEvent(). Fail-safe: publish error is caught and logged, never blocks file write.\n\n3. NEW: tests/orchestra/event-bus.test.ts — 18 tests all passing:\n   - publish→subscribe direct delivery\n   - Channel filter (NOTIFY only skips PHASE)\n   - SprintId filter (sprint-144 sub ignores sprint-145)\n   - Unsubscribe stops delivery\n   - Exception swallowing (sync + async)\n   - tail() last N events, empty file, missing file, malformed lines\n   - writeEvent() integration (singleton eventBus receives events)\n   - unwatchAll cleanup\n   - Multiple subscribers\n   - Wildcard sprintId\n   - subscriberCount diagnostic\n   - watchFile cross-process detection (integration)\n   - EventEmitter raw 'event' emission\n\nVerification: tsc --noEmit PASS, 18/18 tests PASS, 22/22 existing event-stream tests PASS (zero regression). Pre-existing event-stream-emit.test.ts failures confirmed unrelated (8 failures exist on master without our changes).",
